  <diagram id="ecg-paper-f01-offline-plan" name="Offline ReusePlan construction and the measured-ROI boundary" ecgTitle="Offline ReusePlan construction and the measured-ROI boundary" ecgDescription="A left-to-right band shows CSR rows entering a deterministic future-use pass that ranks property vertices by request count, selects the next two accesses to the same property block, and quantizes them into epochs. The resulting edge-aligned ReusePlan crosses an explicit measured-ROI boundary: construction happens before the region of interest, and the kernel only streams validated records inside it.">
